# cross-relay forward-out never binds from_alias to the verified signer - authenticated peers can spoof the sender cross-relay

## Steps to Reproduce

1. TODO: Add steps

## Expected Behavior

TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

## Symptom

Cross-relay forwarded sends never bind from_alias to the verified signer. The verified_alias versus from_alias check exists only in the local-delivery else branch (relay.ml:5577-5579; the forward-out path responds before reaching it). When to_alias carries a non-local host and a peer relay is configured, the request is signed with THIS relays identity and forwarded with the body from_alias verbatim: any authenticated peer (verified as alice) can send to victim@peer2 with from_alias bob, and the peer relay delivers it as bob because relay-to-relay trust substitutes for sender binding. Local sends enforce the binding; the forward-out path omits it.

## Fix direction

Hoist the alias-mismatch rejection above the host-routing branch so it applies to forwarded sends too.

## Evidence

Server-core review 2026-09-17; verified in source by coordinator (check at 5578 is inside the local else arm only).